Correction: Keycloak 26's client list view omits default-valued mapper config keys (userinfo.token.claim), so the realm compatibility check always failed on existing realms (verified against the mothership cluster). getClients now fetches each client's full representation; the test fake reproduces the list-view stripping. Found during the T29 production deploy: the realm had to be re-imported via the designed rebuild path, which also rotated signing keys and required an istiod JWKS cache refresh.
